 RHAISTRAT-8006-E009 | Konflux build onboarding for the kagenti-operator image | Implementation (konflux-onboarding) | Kagenti | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-8006-E010 | Konflux build onboarding for AuthBridge sidecar images | Implementation (konflux-onboarding) | Kagenti | P1 |\n| RHAISTRAT-8006-E011 | DSC component controller for kagenti-operator in rhods-operator | Implementation | Platform / ODH Operator | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-8006-E012 | OLM/CSV packaging with RELATED_IMAGE entries for disconnected installation | Implementation | Platform / ODH Operator | P1 |\n| RHAISTRAT-8006-E013 | Dashboard BFF plugin and feature flag for agent views | Implementation | Dashboard | P1 |\n| RHAISTRAT-8006-E014 | QE test plan and E2E validation for component lifecycle and disconnected install | Implementation | QE | P1 |\n| RHAISTRAT-8006-E015 | Documentation for kagenti-operator enablement and the minimal agent image contract | Implementation (docs-authoring) | Docs | P0 |\n\nNew-component note: neither `kagenti-operator` nor `kagenti-extensions` has an\narchitecture context file, so both are treated as new platform components and\nreceive the full onboarding chain (Rule 20): repo-onboarding + license-validation\nin parallel at the start, konflux-onboarding after repo-onboarding, and general\nimplementation after license-validation (parallel with konflux-onboarding).\n\n## Dependency DAG\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    E001 --> E011\n    E002 --> E010\n    E003 --> E013\n    E004 --> E011\n    E005 --> E011\n    E006 --> E009\n    E006 --> E011\n    E007 --> E010\n    E008 --> E011\n    E011 --> E012\n    E011 --> E013\n    E011 --> E014\n    E012 --> E014\n    E006 --> E015\n    E007 --> E015\n    E008 --> E015\n    E009 --> E015\n    E010 --> E015\n    E011 --> E015\n    E012 --> E015\n    E013 --> E015\n    E014 --> E015\n```\n\n## DAG Justification\n\n| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| E001 → E011 | Rule 3 (Investigation gates affected Implementations) | The upstream validation / gap analysis decides whether the operator can be integrated as-is, whether controllers must be deferred, and whether Keycloak is a required runtime dependency — the DSC integration's scope and validation approach change with the outcome (true gate, action=rewrite). |\n| E002 → E010 | Rule 3 | The AuthBridge variant set determines how many Konflux components the onboarding epic must create (true gate, action=rewrite). |\n| E003 → E013 | Rule 3 | Dashboard TP depth (agent-list tab vs standalone section) changes the UI surface and scope of the dashboard epic (true gate, action=rewrite). |\n| E004 → E011 | Rule 3 | Cleanup semantics for user-namespace AgentRuntime CRs on disable determine what the component controller's Removed-state garbage collection must implement (true gate; folded into E011's rewrite gate). |\n| E005 → E011 | Rule 3 | If the parent RFE's OTEL trace sink requirement enters TP scope, operator deployment configuration is added to the component integration (true gate, action=add_remediation). |\n| E006 → E009 | Rule 5 (repo-onboarding → konflux-onboarding serial) | The Konflux pipeline builds from the opendatahub-io midstream fork; the repo must exist first. |\n| E006 → E011 | Rule 6 (repo-onboarding → general implementation serial) | The rhods-operator integration pulls kustomize manifests from the kagenti-operator midstream fork at pinned commits; the fork and pinned manifest path must exist. |\n| E007 → E010 | Rule 5 | AuthBridge images build from the opendatahub-io/kagenti-extensions fork. |\n| E008 → E011 | Rule 9 (license-validation → general implementation serial) | The DSC component integration ships kagenti artifacts inside the product; a license failure would change the dependencies being integrated. |\n| E011 → E012 | Rule 13 (artifact consumer serial) | The CSV must declare the KagentiOperator CRD and component RBAC that the rhods-operator integration epic produces. |\n| E011 → E013 | Rule 13 (artifact consumer serial) | The dashboard feature flag is gated by the kagenti component state in the DataScienceCluster CR — the schema extension the rhods-operator integration produces. |\n| E011 → E014 | Rule 12/13 (consumer of implemented surface) | E2E lifecycle tests exercise the component controller behavior; the thing under test must exist. |\n| E012 → E014 | Rule 13 | Disconnected-install validation exercises the CSV RELATED_IMAGE resolution the packaging epic produces. |\n| E006…E014 → E015 | Rule 11 (docs-authoring blocked by ALL Implementation epics) | Documentation is always last; it describes the onboarded repos, images, DSC enablement, packaging, dashboard behavior, and validated lifecycle that the other epics produce. |\n\nDeliberately absent edges (Rule 10 / Rule 13 exception):\n\n- No edge from either konflux-onboarding epic (E009/E010) to the DSC component\n  integration (E011), CSV packaging (E012), or dashboard (E013). Build-pipeline\n  onboarding runs in parallel with general implementation; coupling is enforced\n  by \"build pipeline green\" and \"pinned image digest available\" acceptance\n  criteria, never by DAG edges.\n- No edge from the konflux-onboarding epics to the CSV epic for the\n  `RELATED_IMAGE_*` digests: an image digest is a configuration reference filled\n  in at execution time (AC gate on E012), not a build-against artifact.\n- No edge between the two repo-onboarding epics, between license-validation and\n  either repo-onboarding or konflux-onboarding (Rules 7/8: parallel), or between\n  the rhods-operator and dashboard repos' independent work beyond the shared\n  DSC-schema artifact.\n\n## HLR Traceability Matrix\n\n| HLR | Priority | Epics |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Operator images built via Konflux with FIPS-compliant Go compilation on UBI9 | P0 | E009 (primary), E006 (enabler) |\n| Operator enabled/disabled via DataScienceCluster CR, standard component controller pattern, Managed/Removed | P0 | E011 |\n| Full resource cleanup when managementState: Removed | P0 