nce Criteria\n\n- A gap-analysis document exists that gives a pass/fail verdict for each of the three controllers listed in overlay 0014, with evidence\n- The Keycloak question is answered with evidence: is it a required runtime dependency, and can ClientRegistrationController be disabled for TP\n- The midstream fork state (exists, synced, sync process documented) is confirmed or remediation is identified\n- A remediation estimate is recorded, with scope-reduction options if gaps exceed the strategy's threshold\n- The document is shared with the platform integration team before component controller implementation begins\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- Enables the P0 HLRs for DSC component integration (Managed/Removed lifecycle, cleanup, TP opt-in) by determining what the integration deploys and validates\n- Resolves the strategy's critical sprint-1 assumption (\"functional upstream kagenti-operator exists — needs validation\")\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":65686,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-876646f88dda0deb","agent_id":"a21445d56d263f283","session_id":"5aaaeded-1f18-481f-917f-f792958e6a2c","uuid":"94c433e7-7f2e-43f9-a266-f1d454e99ceb","timestamp":"2026-10-22T07:47:14.341Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8006"}
