ntRuntime CRs from the user's accessible namespaces, show status, link to workload details\n- Follow the platform FIPS posture for the Go BFF build (`CGO_ENABLED=1`, strict FIPS runtime tags)\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given the dashboard deployed with the kagenti plugin enabled (feature flag active), a user navigating to the agent views sees a list of AgentRuntime CRs from their accessible namespaces, measured by the dashboard rendering AgentRuntime data retrieved via the BFF API proxy\n- Given the kagenti-operator component is `Removed` in the DSC, the dashboard hides all agent-related UI elements\n- The BFF sidecar runs on a dedicated port with no collision with existing Module Federation ports\n- The BFF enforces the dashboard's standard authentication and authorization model (Bearer token validation, SubjectAccessReviews)\n- The agent views match the decided Tech Preview integration depth and read-only scope\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- P1 HLR: Dashboard integration infrastructure: BFF plugin registration and feature flag for agent views\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":71251,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-876646f88dda0deb","agent_id":"a21445d56d263f283","session_id":"5aaaeded-1f18-481f-917f-f792958e6a2c","uuid":"93876724-ed79-4081-b400-781ca485bed8","timestamp":"2026-10-22T07:48:37.019Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8006"}
