{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-976693b5aed85478","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8006-E001\n3\ttitle: Validate upstream kagenti-operator functionality and runtime dependencies\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8006\n5\tcomponent: Agentic\n6\tteam: Kagenti\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 1\n13\t  local_runnability: 1\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n15\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Validate upstream kagenti-operator functionality and runtime dependencies\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tResolve whether the upstream kagenti-operator (kagenti GitHub org) is functional enough to productize for Tech Preview, and determine its runtime dependency posture. This investigation produces a gap-analysis document that the platform integration work depends on: the strategy's effort estimate (L vs XL), the controller set that ships in TP, and the operator's deployment prerequisites all hinge on its outcome.\n30\t\n31\t## Scope\n32\t\n33\t- Validate the upstream kagenti-operator against the controller inventory in architecture context overlay 0014:\n34\t  - AgentRuntimeReconciler, including metadata fetch from the workload's `/.well-known/agent-card.json` endpoint over mTLS and storage in `AgentRuntime.Status.Card`\n35\t  - MLflowReconciler\n36\t  - ClientRegistrationController\n37\t- Determine whether the kagenti-operator requires Keycloak as a runtime dependency, and whether the ClientRegistrationController can be disabled for Tech Preview if Keycloak is not otherwise provided (Keycloak deployment and OAuth2 client registration infrastructure are managed outside this strategy)\n38\t- Confirm the midstream fork `opendatahub-io/kagenti-operator` is set up and synced with upstream (flagged in the strategy assumptions as needing validation)\n39\t- Confirm the AgentRuntime CRD schema (`agent.kagenti.dev/v1alpha1`) is stable enough for TP\n40\t- Produce a gap-analysis document with a remediation estimate; if gaps exceed roughly 2 sprints of work, record scope-reduction options (e.g., defer MLflowReconciler, defer ClientRegistrationController)\n41\t\n42\t## Acceptance Criteria\n43\t\n44\t- A gap-analysis document exists that gives a pass/fail verdict for each of the three controllers listed in overlay 0014, with evidence\n45\t- The Keycloak question is answered with evidence: is it a required runtime dependency, and can ClientRegistrationController be disabled for TP\n46\t- The midstream fork state (exists, synced, sync process documented) is confirmed or remediation is identified\n47\t- A remediation estimate is recorded, with scope-reduction options if gaps exceed the strategy's threshold\n48\t- The document is shared with the platform integration team before component controller implementation begins\n49\t\n50\t## HLR Traceability\n51\t\n52\t- Enables the P0 HLRs for DSC component integration (Managed/Removed lifecycle, cleanup, TP opt-in) by determining what the integration deploys and validates\n53\t- Resolves the strategy's critical sprint-1 assumption (\"functional upstream kagenti-operator exists — needs validation\")\n54\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b8831966e1a3b1fc","agent_id":"a79e5f145260581af","session_id":"5aaaeded-1f18-481f-917f-f792958e6a2c","uuid":"da2a3028-8fdb-44ce-925c-ea4d9934a3c4","timestamp":"2026-10-22T07:51:53.752Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-976693b5aed85478","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8006 decomposition"}
