rectly kept in E009's description and the summary's Health\n157\tWarnings rather than misfiled as an AC. No epic body references sibling epics by bare\n158\tdraft ID (grep-verified) — epic bodies say \"the decided cleanup semantics\" / \"the\n159\tupstream validation\" instead, which is the correct Jira-safe phrasing.\n160\t\n161\t### 7. Completeness (2/2)\n162\t\n163\tEvery in-scope item has an owner: Konflux builds (E009/E010), component controller\n164\t(E011), OLM/CSV (E012), dashboard visibility (E013), QE (E014), docs (E015); the fork\n165\tenablement work the strategy assumes is explicit in E006/E007. All seven proposed\n166\tacceptance criteria map to epics (AC1/3→E011, AC2→E014's label-application E2E, AC4→E009,\n167\tAC5→E010, AC6→E013, AC7→E012/E014). NFRs are carried: FIPS (E009/E010/E013), container\n168\tsecurity (E009/E010 scope), disconnected install (E012/E014), default-Removed\n169\tcompatibility (E011 AC), cleanup enumeration (E011/E014). Strategy risks and assumptions\n170\tare distributed to the right epics rather than dropped: upstream-gap validation (E001),\n171\twebhook ordering and orphaned-resource risks (E014), port collision (E013), RBAC\n172\tcoexistence assumption (E011 AC), Konflux lead time (E009 description + Health Warnings).\n173\tThe runtime-behavior MUSTs (discovery, metadata sync, degraded conditions, sandbox\n174\tauto-registration) are correctly excluded as RHAIRFE-7587/7588/7589 scope, with the\n175\texclusion documented in Health Warnings rather than silent. Documentation Support is\n176\trequired and E015 exists (Rule 11). No conditional branches were created, and the\n177\tsummary justifies why (each open outcome reshapes an epic that exists in every outcome —\n178\ta rewrite/add_remediation gate, not an epic-set selection), which is the correct\n179\ttreatment for all four bounded outcomes here.\n180\t\n181\tNote (not scored): the strategy's Success Criteria (3 early-access customers,\n182\tminutes-to-discoverable) are TP