{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-83010b77139f9e27","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8006\n3\tepic_count: 15\n4\tcritical_path_length: 5\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\ttriage: null\n7\ttriage_rationale: null\n8\t---\n9\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-8006: Productize & Downstream the Agent Operator\n10\t\n11\t## Triage\n12\t\n13\tFull decomposition (not below-threshold, not docs-only): the strategy spans four\n14\taffected components across three development teams plus QE and Docs, with an L\n15\t(6–9 sprints) effort estimate and multiple architecturally distinct work\n16\tstreams (two Go image build onboarding chains, a platform operator component\n17\tcontroller, OLM/CSV packaging, a dashboard BFF plugin, E2E validation, and\n18\tdocumentation).\n19\t\n20\t## Epic List\n21\t\n22\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n23\t| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n24\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E001 | Validate upstream kagenti-operator functionality and runtime dependencies | Investigation | Kagenti | P0 |\n25\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E002 | Determine AuthBridge sidecar variant set for Tech Preview | Investigation | Kagenti | P1 |\n26\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E003 | Decide dashboard Tech Preview integration depth | Investigation | Dashboard | P1 |\n27\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E004 | Decide AgentRuntime CR cleanup semantics on component disable | Investigation | Platform / ODH Operator | P0 |\n28\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E005 | Resolve OTEL trace sink integration scope for Tech Preview | Investigation | Kagenti | P0 |\n29\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E006 | Establish kagenti-operator midstream fork under opendatahub-io | Implementation (repo-onboarding) | Kagenti | P0 |\n30\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E007 | Establish kagenti-extensions midstream fork under opendatahub-io | Implementation (repo-onboarding) | Kagenti | P1 |\n31\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E008 | License validation for kagenti midstream components | Implementation (license-validation) | Kagenti | P0 |\n32\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E009 | Konflux build onboarding for the kagenti-operator image | Implementation (konflux-onboarding) | Kagenti | P0 |\n33\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E010 | Konflux build onboarding for AuthBridge sidecar images | Implementation (konflux-onboarding) | Kagenti | P1 |\n34\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E011 | DSC component controller for kagenti-operator in rhods-operator | Implementation | Platform / ODH Operator | P0 |\n35\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E012 | OLM/CSV packaging with RELATED_IMAGE entries for disconnected installation | Implementation | Platform / ODH Operator | P1 |\n36\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E013 | Dashboard BFF plugin and feature flag for agent views | Implementation | Dashboard | P1 |\n37\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E014 | QE test plan and E2E validation for component lifecycle and disconnected install | Implementation | QE | P1 |\n38\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E015 | Documentation for kagenti-operator enablement and the minimal agent image contract | Implementation (docs-authoring) | Docs | P0 |\n39\t\n40\tNew-component note: neither `kagenti-operator` nor `kagenti-extensions` has an\n41\tarchitecture context file, so both are treated as new platform components and\n42\treceive the full onboarding chain (Rule 20): repo-onboarding + license-validation\n43\tin parallel at the start, konflux-onboarding after repo-onboarding, and general\n44\timplementation after license-validation (parallel with konflux-onboarding).\n45\t\n46\t## Dependency DAG\n47\t\n48\t```mermaid\n49\tgraph TD\n50\t    E001 --> E011\n51\t    E002 --> E010\n52\t    E003 --> E013\n53\t    E004 --> E011\n54\t    E005 --> E011\n55\t    E006 --> E009\n56\t    E006 --> E011\n57\t    E007 --> E010\n58\t    E008 --> E011\n59\t    E011 --> E012\n60\t    E011 --> E013\n61\t    E011 --> E014\n62\t    E012 --> E014\n63\t    E006 --> E015\n64\t    E007 --> E015\n65\t    E008 --> E015\n66\t    E009 --> E015\n67\t    E010 --> E015\n68\t    E011 --> E015\n69\t    E012 --> E015\n70\t    E013 --> E015\n71\t    E014 --> E015\n72\t```\n73\t\n74\t## DAG Justification\n75\t\n76\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n77\t| --- | --- | --- |\n78\t| E001 → E011 | Rule 3 (Investigation gates affected Implementations) | The upstream validation / gap analysis decides whether the operator can be integrated as-is, whether controllers must be deferred, and whether Keycloak is a required runtime dependency — the DSC integration's scope and validation approach change with the outcome (true gate, action=rewrite). |\n79\t| E002 → E010 | Rule 3 | The AuthBridge variant set determines how many Konflux components the onboarding epic must create (true gate, action=rewrite). |\n80\t| E003 → E013 | Rule 3 | Dashboard TP depth (agent-list tab vs standalone section) changes the UI surface and scope of the dashboard epic (true gate, action=rewrite). |\n81\t| E004 → E011 | Rule 3 | Cleanup semantics for user-namespace AgentRuntime CRs on disable determine what the component controller's Removed-state garbage collection must implement (true gate; folded into E011's rewrite gate). |\n82\t| E005 → E011 | Rule 3 | If the parent RFE's OTEL trace sink requirement enters TP scope, operator deployment configuration is added to the component integration (true gate, action=add_remediation). |\n83\t| E006 → E009 | Rule 5 (repo-onboarding → konflux-onboarding serial) | The Konflux pipeline builds from the opendatahub-io midstream fork; the repo must exist first. |\n84\t| E006 → E011 | Rule 6 (repo-onboarding → general implementation serial) | The rhods-operator integration pulls kustomize manifests from the kagenti-operator midstream fork at pinned commits; the fork and pinned manifest path must exist. |\n85\t| E007 → E010 | Rule 5 | AuthBridge images build from the opendatahub-io/kagenti-extensions fork. |\n86\t| E008 → E011 | Rule 9 (license-validation → general implementation serial) | The DSC component integration ships kagenti artifacts inside the product; a license failure would change the dependencies being integrated. |\n87\t| E011 → E012 | Rule 13 (artifact consumer serial) | The CSV must declare the KagentiOperator CRD and component RBAC that the rhods-operator integration epic produces. |\n88\t| E011 → E013 | Rule 13 (artifact consumer serial) | The dashboard feature flag is gated by the kagenti component state in the DataScienceCluster CR — the schema extension the rhods-operator integration produces. |\n89\t| E011 → E014 | Rule 12/13 (consumer of implemented surface) | E2E lifecycle tests exercise the component controller behavior; the thing under test must exist. |\n90\t| E012 → E014 | Rule 13 | Disconnected-install validation exercises the CSV RELATED_IMAGE resolution the packaging epic produces. |\n91\t| E006…E014 → E015 | Rule 11 (docs-authoring blocked by ALL Implementation epics) | Documentation is always last; it describes the onboarded repos, images, DSC enablement, packaging, dashboard behavior, and validated lifecycle that the other epics produce. |\n92\t\n93\tDeliberately absent edges (Rule 10 / Rule 13 exception):\n94\t\n95\t- No edge from either konflux-onboarding epic (E009/E010) to the DSC component\n96\t  integration (E011), CSV packaging (E012), or dashboard (E013). Build-pipeline\n97\t  onboarding runs in parallel with general implementation; coupling is enforced\n98\t  by \"build pipeline green\" and \"pinned image digest available\" acceptance\n99\t  criteria, never by DAG edges.\n100\t- No edge from the konflux-onboarding epics to the CSV epic for the\n101\t  `RELATED_IMAGE_*` digests: an image digest is a configuration reference filled\n102\t  in at execution time (AC gate on E012), not a build-against artifact.\n103\t- No edge between the two repo-onboarding epics, between license-validation and\n104\t  either repo-onboarding or konflux-onboarding (Rules 7/8: parallel), or between\n105\t  the rhods-operator and dashboard repos' independent work beyond the shared\n106\t  DSC-schema artifact.\n107\t\n108\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n109\t\n110\t| HLR | Priority | Epics |\n111\t| --- | --- | --- |\n112\t| Operator images built via Konflux with FIPS-compliant Go compilation on UBI9 | P0 | E009 (primary), E006 (enabler) |\n113\t| Operator enabled/disabled via DataScienceCluster CR, standard component controller pattern, Managed/Removed | P0 | E011 |\n114\t| Full resource cleanup when managementState: Removed | P0 | E011 (implementation), E004 (semantics decision), E014 (E2E validation) |\n115\t| Upstream-first policy (kagenti/* before opendatahub-io/* midstream) | P0 | E006, E007 (fork + sync process), enforced as ACs on E009/E010 |\n116\t| Tech Preview maturity, explicit opt-in (disabled by default in DSC) | P0 | E011 |\n117\t| Dashboard integration infrastructure: BFF plugin registration and feature flag | P1 | E013 |\n118\t| OLM/CSV packaging with RELATED_IMAGE_* entries for disconnected installation | P1 | E012 (E009/E010 produce the referenced images; digests are AC-gated config refs) |\n119\t| AuthBridge proxy sidecar image built via Konflux with FIPS compliance | P1 | E010 (primary), E007 (enabler), E002 (variant decision) |\n120\t| Multi-arch builds (AMD64 required; arm64 if pipeline supports it without additional effort) | P2 | E009, E010 (acceptance criteria) |\n121\t\n122\tStrategy-level acceptance criterion \"Documentation covers the minimal image\n123\tcontract for creating a discoverable agent\" is covered by E015.\n124\t\n125\tRFE-level runtime acceptance criteria (agent discovery via AgentRuntime\n126\ttargetRef selection, metadata verification on rollouts, degraded conditions on\n127\tunreachable A2A endpoints, sandbox auto-registration) are delivered by the\n128\tupstream operator's runtime behavior and are explicitly out of scope for this\n129\tstrategy (tracked by RHAIRFE-7587/7588/7589) — see Health Warnings.\n130\t\n131\t## Health Warnings\n132\t\n133\t- **Pending human reviews gate the whole strategy**: Architecture Review, Build\n134\t  Onboarding, License Validation, Documentation Support, and UXD Support are all\n135\t  \"Pending human review\" in the strategy's prerequisites table, and the Jira\n136\t  labels include `ac-review-pending` and `confidence-yellow`. Nothing in this\n137\t  DAG can substitute for those sign-offs.\n138\t- **Konflux submission lead time is a schedule risk, not an AC**: the risk table\n139\t  flags onboarding lead time against the code-complete deadline (submit\n140\t  immediately, escalate if delayed past 2 weeks before deadline). Captured as a\n141\t  risk note on the konflux-onboarding epics, not as an acceptance criterion.\n142\t- **Runtime acceptance criteria live outside this strategy**: the RFE-level\n143\t  MUSTs for discovery, metadata sync, and degraded conditions, and the COULD for\n144\t  sandbox auto-registration, are runtime operator behavior covered by\n145\t  RHAIRFE-7587/7588. No epic in this decomposition implements them; reviewers\n146\t  should not expect them here.\n147\t- **Top-level open questions treated as resolved or out of scope**: the\n148\t  pre-strategy \"Open Questions\" section asks about the minimal image contract\n149\t  format (A2A vs simpler) and the OpenShell Sandbox CR interaction. The refined\n150\t  technical approach pins the contract (capability description at\n151\t  `/.well-known/agent-card.json`, fetched by AgentRuntimeReconciler over mTLS,\n152\t  stored in AgentRuntime.Status.Card), and the Sandbox CR interaction is runtime\n153\t  behavior outside this strategy's productization scope. Neither changes the\n154\t  epic set; both are noted for the review record.\n155\t- **Priority observation**: the AuthBridge image HLR is P1 even though sidecar\n156\t  injection is part of the operator's TP function; this follows the strategy's\n157\t  own labels and is not an inversion introduced by decomposition.\n158\t- **Multiple gates on the DSC integration epic**: E011 is gated by three\n159\t  investigations (upstream validation, cleanup semantics, OTEL scope). The\n160\t  frontmatter `gated_by