{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-94436d17399b2900","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8006-E004\n3\ttitle: Decide AgentRuntime CR cleanup semantics on component disable\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8006\n5\tcomponent: AI Core Platform\n6\tteam: Platform / ODH Operator\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 1\n13\t  local_runnability: 0\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: 0\n15\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Decide AgentRuntime CR cleanup semantics on component disable\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tDecide what happens to user-created AgentRuntime CRs in user namespaces when the kagenti-operator component is disabled in the DataScienceCluster CR (`managementState: Removed`). The component controller cleans up operator-managed resources in `redhat-ods-applications`, but user-created CRs in other namespaces may become orphaned, and deleting user data across namespaces is a destructive semantic that must be decided deliberately before the cleanup logic is implemented.\n30\t\n31\t## Scope\n32\t\n33\t- Decide whether Removed-state cleanup includes cross-namespace deletion of the AgentRuntime CRD (which garbage-collects user-created CRs cluster-wide) or leaves user-created CRs in place\n34\t- Align the decision with the garbage-collection pattern used by the existing rhods-operator component controllers (architecture context: rhods-operator.md component action pipeline)\n35\t- Record guidance for the component controller implementation, including how orphaned resources are handled and how the behavior is communicated to users\n36\t\n37\t## Acceptance Criteria\n38\t\n39\t- A written decision defines exactly which resources are deleted on Managed → Removed transition, including the disposition of user-created AgentRuntime CRs in user namespaces\n40\t- The decision is consistent with the platform's existing component-controller cleanup pattern or documents why it diverges\n41\t\n42\t## HLR Traceability\n43\t\n44\t- Gates the P0 HLR \"When disabled (managementState: Removed), all operator-managed resources are cleaned up\" by defining the boundary of \"operator-managed\" for user-namespace CRs\n45\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bfa115eb70992148","agent_id":"af7944a590e02bfb7","session_id":"5aaaeded-1f18-481f-917f-f792958e6a2c","uuid":"014d5ae0-64a7-48ed-aaea-b323c5125644","timestamp":"2026-10-22T07:59:37.672Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-94436d17399b2900","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8006 decomposition"}
