{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-982098000d237a1b","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8006-E006\n3\ttitle: Establish kagenti-operator midstream fork under opendatahub-io\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8006\n5\tcomponent: Agentic\n6\tteam: Kagenti\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\timplementation_type: repo-onboarding\n10\tdependencies: []\n11\tai_signals:\n12\t  change_specificity: 1\n13\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n14\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n15\t  existing_foundation: 1\n16\t  open_questions: 0\n17\t  external_dependency: 0\n18\t  human_process_gates: 0\n19\t  repo_access: 1\n20\t  architecture_claims: 0\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 4\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Establish kagenti-operator midstream fork under opendatahub-io\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tEstablish and sync the midstream fork of the upstream kagenti-operator (`kagenti/kagenti-operator` → `opendatahub-io/kagenti-operator`) so that Konflux builds and the platform's component integration have a controlled, pinned source. The kagenti-operator is a new platform component (no architecture context file exists for it), so it requires the full midstream onboarding chain.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Establish the `opendatahub-io/kagenti-operator` midstream fork (create/confirm the repo under the opendatahub-io GitHub org) with content synced from upstream\n38\t- Document the fork sync process (how upstream releases are pulled into midstream at pinned commits)\n39\t- Provide a pinned-commit manifest retrieval path (the `get_all_manifests.sh` mechanism used by rhods-operator component integrations) so kustomize manifests can be pulled at pinned commits into `prefetched-manifests/kagenti-operator/`\n40\t- Apply the upstream-first policy: significant changes go to `kagenti/*` upstream repos before being pulled into the opendatahub-io midstream fork, and the fork's contribution flow documents this\n41\t\n42\t## Acceptance Criteria\n43\t\n44\t- The `opendatahub-io/kagenti-operator` midstream fork exists and is synced with the upstream `kagenti/kagenti-operator` at a pinned commit\n45\t- The fork sync process is documented and repeatable\n46\t- Manifests are retrievable from the midstream fork at pinned commits via the standard retrieval script\n47\t\n48\t## HLR Traceability\n49\t\n50\t- P0 HLR: Upstream-first policy — significant changes go to `kagenti/*` repos before being pulled into `opendatahub-io/*` midstream forks (the fork and its sync/contribution flow implement this policy)\n51\t- Enables the P0 HLR for Konflux-built operator images (the pipeline builds from this fork)\n52\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bfa115eb70992148","agent_id":"af7944a590e02bfb7","session_id":"5aaaeded-1f18-481f-917f-f792958e6a2c","uuid":"1aeb9ef3-761a-4d08-8dbd-1d60b83836c8","timestamp":"2026-10-22T07:59:41.992Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-982098000d237a1b","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8006 decomposition"}
