{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a0ff3d8345f5f220","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8006-E013\n3\ttitle: Dashboard BFF plugin and feature flag for agent views\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8006\n5\tcomponent: AI Core Dashboard\n6\tteam: Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8006-E003\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8006-E011\n12\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8006-E003\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: rewrite\n15\t  fallback_approach: If a standalone navigation section is chosen instead of a minimal\n16\t    agent-list tab, the UI surface and effort expand (roughly 1 to 2 sprints) and\n17\t    the BFF scope changes accordingly.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 0\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: -1\n24\t  external_dependency: 0\n25\t  human_process_gates: -1\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 3\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\tbranch: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Dashboard BFF plugin and feature flag for agent views\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tRegister a kagenti dashboard plugin in the odh-dashboard Module Federation architecture: a new Go BFF container that proxies Kubernetes API requests for AgentRuntime CR management, plus a feature flag in the OdhDashboardConfig CR that hides all agent-related UI when the kagenti-operator component is `Removed` in the DSC. Tech Preview scope is read-only agent visibility: list AgentRuntime CRs, show status, and link to workload details; full agent management UI is out of scope.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Implement a new Go BFF container following the pattern of the existing federated modules (gen-ai-ui, maas-ui, and others), proxying requests to the Kubernetes API for AgentRuntime CR management, including Bearer token validation and SubjectAccessReview-based authorization consistent with the other BFF sidecars\n44\t- Run the BFF as a sidecar container in the dashboard pod on a dedicated port (next available in the 8043-8743 range, verified against current assignments: 8043-model-registry, 8143-gen-ai, 8243-maas, 8343-mlflow, 8443-eval-hub, 8543-automl, 8643-autorag)\n45\t- Register the UI module via Module Federation and the federation configmap path mapping\n46\t- Add a `disableKagenti` feature flag (or equivalent) to the OdhDashboardConfig CR, gated by the kagenti-operator component state in the DSC; when the component is `Removed`, the dashboard hides all agent-related UI elements\n47\t- Build the read-only agent list view per the decided Tech Preview integration depth (agent-list tab in an existing project view vs standalone navigation section): list AgentRuntime CRs from the user's accessible namespaces, show status, link to workload details\n48\t- Follow the platform FIPS posture for the Go BFF build (`CGO_ENABLED=1`, strict FIPS runtime tags)\n49\t\n50\t## Acceptance Criteria\n51\t\n52\t- Given the dashboard deployed with the kagenti plugin enabled (feature flag active), a user navigating to the agent views sees a list of AgentRuntime CRs from their accessible namespaces, measured by the dashboard rendering AgentRuntime data retrieved via the BFF API proxy\n53\t- Given the kagenti-operator component is `Removed` in the DSC, the dashboard hides all agent-related UI elements\n54\t- The BFF sidecar runs on a dedicated port with no collision with existing Module Federation ports\n55\t- The BFF enforces the dashboard's standard authentication and authorization model (Bearer token validation, SubjectAccessReviews)\n56\t- The agent views match the decided Tech Preview integration depth and read-only scope\n57\t\n58\t## HLR Traceability\n59\t\n60\t- P1 HLR: Dashboard integration infrastructure: BFF plugin registration and feature flag for agent views\n61\t"}]},"p