{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9de0d7bc6891df8a","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8006-E014\n3\ttitle: QE test plan and E2E validation for component lifecycle and disconnected install\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8006\n5\tcomponent: QE\n6\tteam: QE\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8006-E011\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8006-E012\n12\tai_signals:\n13\t  change_specificity: 1\n14\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n15\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n16\t  existing_foundation: 1\n17\t  open_questions: 0\n18\t  external_dependency: 0\n19\t  human_process_gates: 0\n20\t  repo_access: 1\n21\t  architecture_claims: 0\n22\timplementation_type: null\n23\tinvestigation_signals: null\n24\tai_implementability: High\n25\tai_implementability_score: 4\n26\tjira_key: null\n27\tbranch: null\n28\tgated_by: null\n29\tgate_failure_impact: null\n30\t---\n31\t# QE test plan and E2E validation for component lifecycle and disconnected install\n32\t\n33\t## Description\n34\t\n35\tCreate the QE test plan and E2E test suite validating the kagenti-operator's productization: DSC component lifecycle (Managed/Removed including full cleanup), webhook interaction with other platform mutating webhooks, and disconnected installation using mirrored images.\n36\t\n37\t## Scope\n38\t\n39\t- Test plan covering the kagenti-operator component lifecycle, disconnected installation, and webhook ordering\n40\t- E2E tests for the DSC component lifecycle: `Managed` deploys a Ready kagenti-operator Deployment in `redhat-ods-applications`; `Managed` → `Removed` deletes all operator-managed resources (Deployment, RBAC, CRDs, webhook configuration), including resources in multiple namespaces, consistent with the decided cleanup semantics — no orphaned AgentRuntime CRs or webhook configurations persist after disable\n41\t- E2E coverage for the AgentRuntime onboarding flow at the productization level: a user creates an AgentRuntime CR referencing an existing Deployment and the operator applies the `kagenti.io/type: agent` label to the target workload\n42\t- Webhook ordering tests: the kagenti mutating webhook (with `reinvocationPolicy: IfNeeded`) coexisting with other platform mutating webhooks (HardwareProfile, connection injection) without pod creation failures; set explicit `webhookOrder` annotations if conflicts arise\n43\t- Disconnected-install validation: with image mirroring, the operator and AuthBridge images resolve from the mirrored registry via the CSV `RELATED_IMAGE_*` entries\n44\t- E2E suite runs against Konflux-built images (pinned digests available — a configuration gate, not a build dependency)\n45\t\n46\t## Acceptance Criteria\n47\t\n48\t- The test plan is written and reviewed\n49\t- The E2E suite passes against a deployment using Konflux-built images: lifecycle, cleanup (multi-namespace), and AgentRuntime label application\n50\t- The webhook ordering scenario passes alongside the platform's other mutating webhooks (or explicit `webhookOrder` annotations are applied and documented)\n51\t- The disconnected-install scenario demonstrates the kagenti-operator Deployment running with images resolved from the mirror registry\n52\t\n53\t## HLR Traceability\n54\t\n55\t- Validates the P0 HLRs for DSC enablement/disable and full cleanup on `Removed`\n56\t- Validates the P1 HLR for OLM/CSV packaging with `RELATED_IMAGE_*` entries for disconnected installation\n57\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bfa115eb70992148","agent_id":"af7944a590e02bfb7","session_id":"5aaaeded-1f18-481f-917f-f792958e6a2c","uuid":"e69db921-c9db-4aeb-99dc-23a9d6b601db","timestamp":"2026-10-22T07:59:52.038Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9de0d7bc6891df8a","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8006 decomposition"}
