rom\n31\t    the DAG.'\n32\t- severity: minor\n33\t  criterion: Epic Boundaries\n34\t  description: E011 carries the strategy full 2-3 sprint rhods-operator component-controller\n35\t    estimate (CRD, DSC schema extension, controller, kustomize integration, cleanup\n36\t    logic) - at/above the ~2-week epic guideline. Defensibly kept whole as one pattern-following\n37\t    logical change for one component and team, but it is the largest epic in the set.\n38\terror: null\n39\t---\n40\t# Decomposition Review — RHAISTRAT-8006\n41\t\n42\t## Review Summary\n43\t\n44\tScore: 10/14 — fail\n45\tRecommendation: revise\n46\t\n47\tContract validator: OK (`validate_decomposition.py` exited 0 — epic body sections,\n48\tcanonical component names, Rule 11 docs-last coverage, and priority inheritance\n49\tall pass). Triage consistency: `triage: null` (full decomposition) with 15 epics —\n50\tno contradiction. The failure below is a DAG completeness issue the validator\n51\tcannot see.\n52\t\n53\t## Criterion Details\n54\t\n55\t### 1. HLR Coverage (2/2)\n56\t\n57\tAll nine HLRs (5×P0, 3×P1, 1×P2) map to epics in the traceability matrix and in\n58\teach epic's HLR Traceability section. P2 multi-arch is covered as ACs on E009/E010\n59\t— correct handling: the AMD64 requirement is inseparable from the Konflux build and\n60\tthe arm64 clause is incidental to the same build surface, not a deferrable feature,\n61\tso bundling is right.\n62\t\n63\tPriority inheritance verified by enumerating every dependency list: E011 (P0) is\n64\tblocked only by P0 epics (E001, E004, E005, E006, E008); E010 (P1) by E002/E007\n65\t(P1); E013 (P1) by E003 (P1) and E011 (P0); E012/E014 (P1) by E011 (P0) and each\n66\tother appropriately. E015 (docs-authoring, P0) is exempt from inheritance and\n67\tcorrectly derives P0 from the strategy's Critical priority; its dependencies on P1\n68\tepics are not violations. No priority collapse with deferrable features.\n69\t\n70\t### 2. DAG Coherence (0/2)\n71\t\n72\t