endencies`, and each has a populated `gate_failure_impact` with both `action`\n131\tand `fallback_approach`.\n132\t\n133\tGap: E011 lists Investigations E004 and E005 in `dependencies` without `gated_by`.\n134\tThe epic-level schema's `gated_by` is single-valued, so only the primary gate\n135\t(E001) is recorded; the summary discloses this and enumerates all three gate\n136\toutcomes in `gate_failure_impact.fallback_approach`, so scheduling execution is\n137\tunaffected — but two of E011's three true gates are not machine-readable as gates,\n138\twhich is exactly the metadata condition this criterion scores at 1.\n139\t\n140\t### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (1/2)\n141\t\n142\tSignal fields are type-correct everywhere (Implementation epics carry `ai_signals`,\n143\tInvestigation epics carry `investigation_signals`; no cross-assignment). All 15\n144\tai-signals files exist, are substantial, and their rationales match the frontmatter\n145\tvalues. Investigation signals are well-judged: E001's `source_accessibility: 1`\n146\t(answerable from readable repos) vs E002/E003/E005's `0` with\n147\t`human_judgment_required: -2` (pending PM/team decisions) is exactly the right\n148\tdistinction.\n149\t\n150\tOne arguable value: E012 scores `open_questions: 0` while its own rationale\n151\tacknowledges the additional AuthBridge variant entries depend on the unresolved TP\n152\tvariant decision — the same uncertainty is scored `-1` on E010. The \"entries are\n153\tadditive\" reasoning is defensible, but it underplays the E002 dependency that is\n154\talso missing from the DAG (see Criterion 2). Arithmetic/thresholds not checked per\n155\tinstructions.\n156\t\n157\t### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\n158\t\n159\tRule-mandated ACs verified on every applicable epic: E009 and E010 both carry the\n160\tKonflux `check-payload` FIPS AC (Rule 25 chain); E011 carries \"build pipeline\n161\tgreen\" plus the pinned-digest configuration gate; E012's digest AC is correctly\n162\tframed as a configuration reference; E015 carries the technical-review AC (Rule\n163\t24). No replacement of an existing capability, so Rule 23 rollback/feature-flag is\n164\tN/A (E013 includes feature-flag behavior ACs anyway). All ACs are testable with\n165\tconcrete measurement (kubectl queries, rendered UI, mirror-registry resolution).\n166\tThe Konflux lead-time schedule constraint is correctly kept out of ACs (Description\n167\t+ Health Warning) — no soft ACs found. No draft-ID references in any epic body\n168\t(verified by grep; only frontmatter dependency lists contain epic IDs).\n169\t\n170\t### 7. Completeness (2/2)\n171\t\n172\tStrategy scope is fully accounted for: Konflux onboarding (E009/E010), DSC\n173\tcomponent controller (E011), OLM/CSV (E012), dashboard BFF (E013), QE (E014), docs\n174\t(E015), with all five strategy open questions mapped to Investigations E001-E005\n175\tand the Keycloak question correctly combined into E001. All seven proposed\n176\tacceptance criteria are covered (the runtime-behavior criteria via E014's\n177\tproductization-level E2E, which is the right home given the strategy's own\n178\tout-of-scope boundaries). Risks are carried forward (webhook ordering → E014, port\n179\tcollision → E013, orphaned resources → E004/E014, Konflux lead time → risk note).\n180\tNFRs are distributed appropriately (FIPS/container security on E009/E010/E013,\n181\tdisconnected install on E012/E014, default-Removed on E011). Documentation Support\n182\tis listed in prerequisites and a docs-authoring epic exists (Rule 11) with correct\n183\tdocs-last dependencies on all nine Implementation epics. No conditional branches,\n184\twith a sound justification (all bounded outcomes change scope of existing epics,\n185\tnot the epic set). Strategy-level context (pending human reviews, OTEL open item,\n186\truntime-AC ownership) is preserved in Health Warnings rather than silently\n187\tdropped.\n188\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ad48c18a4a278ae0",