{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a6893fe78099f0d2","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8006-E011\n3\ttitle: DSC component controller for kagenti-operator in rhods-operator\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8006\n5\tcomponent: AI Core Platform\n6\tteam: Platform / ODH Operator\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8006-E001\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8006-E004\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8006-E005\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-8006-E006\n14\t- RHAISTRAT-8006-E008\n15\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8006-E001\n16\tgate_failure_impact:\n17\t  action: rewrite\n18\t  fallback_approach: If the upstream operator has functional gaps, integration scope\n19\t    changes (defer MLflowReconciler/ClientRegistrationController or add midstream\n20\t    remediation first); if Keycloak is required and cannot be disabled, deployment\n21\t    prerequisites change; if the cleanup-semantics decision excludes cross-namespace\n22\t    deletion of the AgentRuntime CRD, the Removed-state garbage-collection scope changes\n23\t    to match the decided boundary of operator-managed resources; if OTEL trace sink\n24\t    integration enters scope, deployment configuration is added.\n25\tai_signals:\n26\t  change_specificity: 1\n27\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n28\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n29\t  existing_foundation: 1\n30\t  open_questions: -1\n31\t  external_dependency: 0\n32\t  human_process_gates: -1\n33\t  repo_access: 1\n34\t  architecture_claims: 1\n35\timplementation_type: null\n36\tinvestigation_signals: null\n37\tai_implementability: High\n38\tai_implementability_score: 4\n39\tjira_key: null\n40\tbranch: null\n41\t---\n42\t# DSC component controller for kagenti-operator in rhods-operator\n43\t\n44\t## Description\n45\t\n46\tRegister the kagenti-operator as a new standard component managed by the Data Science Cluster (DSC) CR in rhods-operator, following the established component controller pattern (16 existing precedents). This is the core platform integration epic: it makes the kagenti-operator deployable, removable, and observable as a first-class RHOAI component at Tech Preview maturity with explicit opt-in.\n47\t\n48\t## Scope\n49\t\n50\t- Define the `KagentiOperator` component CRD in the `components.platform.opendatahub.io/v1alpha1` group, following the same pattern as `ModelRegistry`, `Trainer`, `FeastOperator`, and other component CRDs\n51\t- Extend the DSC CR schema with the kagenti-operator component\n52\t- Implement the component controller with the standard action pipeline (initialize, releases, kustomize render, deploy, check deployments, garbage collect) and register it in the component registry (`internal/controller/components/registry/`)\n53\t- Support the `managementState` lifecycle: `Managed` (deploy operator + CRDs + RBAC + webhook) and `Removed` (delete the controller Deployment, RBAC resources, CRDs, mutating webhook configuration, and namespace-scoped resources in `redhat-ods-applications`), implementing the cleanup semantics decided for user-namespace AgentRuntime CRs\n54\t- Default to `Removed` for Tech Preview (explicit opt-in), so existing clusters are unaffected by RHOAI upgrade\n55\t- Pull upstream manifests from the kagenti-operator midstream fork at pinned commits into `prefetched-manifests/kagenti-operator/`, with RHOAI-specific kustomize overlays for namespace, image references, and RBAC adjustments\n56\t- Deploy into the `redhat-ods-applications` namespace; the operator watches all namespaces for AgentRuntime CRs\n57\t- Include OTEL trace sink deployment configuration if the Tech Preview scope decision requires it\n58\t- Document runtime prerequisites surfaced by the upstream validation (e.g., Keycloak) in the deployment configuration\n59\t\n60\t## Acceptance Criteria\n61\t\n62\t- Given a fresh RHOAI deployment with the kagenti-operator component set to `managementState: Managed`, the DSC controller reconciles and the kagenti-operator Deployment is created in `redhat-ods-applications` and becomes Ready, measured by `kubectl get deployment -n redhat-ods-applications -l app=kagenti-operator`\n63\t- The Deployment references the Konflux-built kagenti-operator image (SHA256-pinned digest available; build pipeline green) — the image reference is a configuration gate, not a build-against dependency\n64\t- Given the component changed from `Managed` to `Removed`, the component controller reconciles and all operator-managed resources (Deployment, RBAC, CRDs, webhook configuration) are deleted, measured by the Deployment query returning no results and the AgentRuntime CRD returning \"not found\", consistent with the decided cleanup semantics for user-namespace CRs\n65\t- The component defaults to `Removed` (disabled) so existing clusters are unaffected by upgrade\n66\t- The kagenti-operator can run in `redhat-ods-applications` alongside other platform operators without RBAC conflicts (validated in E2E)\n67\t- Build pipeline for rhods-operator changes is green\n68\t\n69\t## HLR Traceability\n70\t\n71\t- P0 HLR: Operator enabled/disabled via DataScienceCluster CR following the standard component controller pattern with `managementState: Managed/Removed`\n72\t- P0 HLR: When disabled (`managementState: Removed`), all operator-managed resources are cleaned up (Deployment, RBAC, CRDs, namespace-scoped resources)\n73\t- P0 HLR: Tech Preview maturity level with explicit opt-in (disabled by default in DSC)\n74\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ad48c18a4a278ae0","agent_id":"a88b627e060c88042","session_id":"5aaaeded-1f18-481f-917f-f792958e6a2c","uuid":"b37a37f9-1c29-4312-b161-c7fac6f7ff96","timestamp":"2026-10-22T08:08:30.867Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a6893fe78099f0d2","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-revise RHAISTRAT-8006 decomposition"}
