{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-973951d2e757cc6a","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8006\n3\tepic_count: 15\n4\tcritical_path_length: 5\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\ttriage: null\n7\ttriage_rationale: null\n8\trevised: true\n9\t---\n10\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-8006: Productize & Downstream the Agent Operator\n11\t\n12\t## Triage\n13\t\n14\tFull decomposition (not below-threshold, not docs-only): the strategy spans four\n15\taffected components across three development teams plus QE and Docs, with an L\n16\t(6–9 sprints) effort estimate and multiple architecturally distinct work\n17\tstreams (two Go image build onboarding chains, a platform operator component\n18\tcontroller, OLM/CSV packaging, a dashboard BFF plugin, E2E validation, and\n19\tdocumentation).\n20\t\n21\t## Epic List\n22\t\n23\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n24\t| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n25\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E001 | Validate upstream kagenti-operator functionality and runtime dependencies | Investigation | Kagenti | P0 |\n26\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E002 | Determine AuthBridge sidecar variant set for Tech Preview | Investigation | Kagenti | P1 |\n27\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E003 | Decide dashboard Tech Preview integration depth | Investigation | Dashboard | P1 |\n28\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E004 | Decide AgentRuntime CR cleanup semantics on component disable | Investigation | Platform / ODH Operator | P0 |\n29\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E005 | Resolve OTEL trace sink integration scope for Tech Preview | Investigation | Kagenti | P0 |\n30\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E006 | Establish kagenti-operator midstream fork under opendatahub-io | Implementation (repo-onboarding) | Kagenti | P0 |\n31\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E007 | Establish kagenti-extensions midstream fork under opendatahub-io | Implementation (repo-onboarding) | Kagenti | P1 |\n32\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E008 | License validation for kagenti midstream components | Implementation (license-validation) | Kagenti | P0 |\n33\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E009 | Konflux build onboarding for the kagenti-operator image | Implementation (konflux-onboarding) | Kagenti | P0 |\n34\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E010 | Konflux build onboarding for AuthBridge sidecar images | Implementation (konflux-onboarding) | Kagenti | P1 |\n35\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E011 | DSC component controller for kagenti-operator in rhods-operator | Implementation | Platform / ODH Operator | P0 |\n36\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E012 | OLM/CSV packaging with RELATED_IMAGE entries for disconnected installation | Implementation | Platform / ODH Operator | P1 |\n37\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E013 | Dashboard BFF plugin and feature flag for agent views | Implementation | Dashboard | P1 |\n38\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E014 | QE test plan and E2E validation for component lifecycle and disconnected install | Implementation | QE | P1 |\n39\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E015 | Documentation for kagenti-operator enablement and the minimal agent image contract | Implementation (docs-authoring) | Docs | P0 |\n40\t\n41\tNew-component note: neither `kagenti-operator` nor `kagenti-extensions` has an\n42\tarchitecture context file, so both are treated as new platform components and\n43\treceive the full onboarding chain (Rule 20): repo-onboarding + license-validation\n44\tin parallel at the start, konflux-onboarding after repo-onboarding, and general\n45\timplementation after license-validation (parallel with konflux-onboarding).\n46\t\n47\t## Dependency DAG\n48\t\n49\t```mermaid\n50\tgraph TD\n51\t    E001 --> E011\n52\t    E002 --> E010\n53\t    E002 --> E012\n54\t    E003 --> E013\n55\t    E004 --> E011\n56\t    E005 --> E011\n57\t    E006 --> E009\n58\t    E006 --> E011\n59\t    E007 --> E010\n60\t    E008 --> E011\n61\t    E011 --> E012\n62\t    E011 --> E013\n63\t    E011 --> E014\n64\t    E012 --> E014\n65\t    E006 --> E015\n66\t    E007 --> E015\n67\t    E008 --> E015\n68\t    E009 --> E015\n69\t    E010 --> E015\n70\t    E011 --> E015\n71\t    E012 --> E015\n72\t    E013 --> E015\n73\t    E014 --> E015\n74\t```\n75\t\n76\t## DAG Justification\n77\t\n78\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n79\t| --- | --- | --- |\n80\t| E001 → E011 | Rule 3 (Investigation gates affected Implementations) | The upstream validation / gap analysis decides whether the operator can be integrated as-is, whether controllers must be deferred, and whether Keycloak is a required runtime dependency — the DSC integration's scope and validation approach change with the outcome (true gate, action=rewrite). |\n81\t| E002 → E010 | Rule 3 | The AuthBridge variant set determines how many Konflux components the onboarding epic must create (true gate, action=rewrite). |\n82\t| E002 → E012 | Rule 3 | The AuthBridge variant set determines which `RELATED_IMAGE_*` entries the CSV packaging epic must add — the entry list expands or contracts with the outcome (true gate, action=rewrite). |\n83\t| E003 → E013 | Rule 3 | Dashboard TP depth (agent-list tab vs standalone section) changes the UI surface and scope of the dashboard epic (true gate, action=rewrite). |\n84\t| E004 → E011 | Rule 3 | Cleanup semantics for user-namespace AgentRuntime CRs on disable determine what the component controller's Removed-state garbage collection must implement (true gate; folded into E011's rewrite gate). |\n85\t| E005 → E011 | Rule 3 | If the parent RFE's OTEL trace sink requirement enters TP scope, operator deployment configuration is added to the component integration (true gate, action=add_remediation). |\n86\t| E006 → E009 | Rule 5 (repo-onboarding → konflux-onboarding serial) | The Konflux pipeline builds from the opendatahub-io midstream fork; the repo must exist first. |\n87\t| E006 → E011 | Rule 6 (repo-onboarding → general implementation serial) | The rhods-operator integration pulls kustomize manifests from the kagenti-operator midstream fork at pinned commits; the fork and pinned manifest path must exist. |\n88\t| E007 → E010 | Rule 5 | AuthBridge images build from the opendatahub-io/kagenti-extensions fork. |\n89\t| E008 → E011 | Rule 9 (license-validation → general implementation serial) | The DSC component integration ships kagenti artifacts inside the product; a license failure would change the dependencies being integrated. |\n90\t| E011 → E012 | Rule 13 (artifact consumer serial) | The CSV must declare the KagentiOperator CRD and component RBAC that the rhods-operator integration epic produces. |\n91\t| E011 → E013 | Rule 13 (artifact consumer serial) | The dashboard feature flag is gated by the kagenti component state in the DataScienceCluster CR — the schema extension the rhods-operator integration produces. |\n92\t| E011 → E014 | Rule 12/13 (consumer of implemented surface) | E2E lifecycle tests exercise the component controller behavior; the thing under test must exist. |\n93\t| E012 → E014 | Rule 13 | Disconnected-install validation exercises the CSV RELATED_IMAGE resolution the packaging epic produces. |\n94\t| E006…E014 → E015 | Rule 11 (docs-authoring blocked by ALL Implementation epics) | Documentation is always last; it describes the onboarded repos, images, DSC enablement, packaging, dashboard behavior, and validated lifecycle that the other epics produce. |\n95\t\n96\tDeliberately absent edges (Rule 10 / Rule 13 exception):\n97\t\n98\t- No edge from either konflux-onboarding epic (E009/E010) to the DSC component\n99\t  integration (E011), CSV packaging (E012), or dashboard (E013). Build-pipeline\n100\t  onboarding runs in parallel with general implementation; coupling is enforced\n101\t  by \"build pipeline green\" and \"pinned image digest available\" acceptance\n102\t  criteria, never by DAG edges.\n103\t- No edge from the konflux-onboarding epics to the CSV epic for the\n104\t  `RELATED_IMAGE_*` digests: an image digest is a configuration reference filled\n105\t  in at execution time (AC gate on E012), not a build-against artifact. This\n106\t  exception covers only the digest references — the *variant-set scope*\n107\t  dependency (which AuthBridge variants are in Tech Preview and therefore need\n108\t  CSV entries) is a Rule 3 edge, E002 → E012, not a digest configuration\n109\t  reference.\n110\t- No edge between the two repo-onboarding epics, between license-validation and\n111\t  either repo-onboarding or konflux-onboarding (Rules 7/8: parallel), or between\n112\t  the rhods-operator and dashboard repos' independent work beyond the shared\n113\t  DSC-schema artifact.\n114\t\n115\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n116\t\n117\t| HLR | Priority | Epics |\n118\t| --- | --- | --- |\n119\t| Operator images built via Konflux with FIPS-compliant Go compilation on UBI9 | P0 | E009 (primary), E006 (enabler) |\n120\t| Operator enabled/disabled via DataScienceCluster CR, standard component controller pattern, Managed/Removed | P0 | E011 |\n121\t| Full resource cleanup when managementState: Removed | P0 | E011 (implementation), E004 (semantics decision), E014 (E2E validation) |\n122\t| Upstream-first policy (kagenti/* before opendatahub-io/* midstream) | P0 | E006, E007 (fork + sync process), enforced as ACs on E009/E010 |\n123\t| Tech Preview maturity, explicit opt-in (disabled by default in DSC) | P0 | E011 |\n124\t| Dashboard integration infrastructure: BFF plugin registration and feature flag | P1 | E013 |\n125\t| OLM/CSV packaging with RELATED_IMAGE_* entries for disconnected installation | P1 | E012 (E009/E010 produce the referenced images; digests are AC-gated config refs; E002 fixes the variant entry list) |\n126\t| AuthBridge proxy sidecar image built via Konflux with FIPS compliance | P1 | E010 (primary), E007 (enabler), E002 (variant decision) |\n127\t| Multi-arch builds (AMD64 required; arm64 if pipeline supports it without additional effort) | P2 | E009, E010 (acceptance criteria) |\n128\t\n129\tStrategy-level acceptance criterion \"Documentation covers the minimal image\n130\tcontract for creating a discoverable agent\" is covered by E015.\n131\t\n132\tRFE-level runtime acceptance criteria (agent discovery via AgentRuntime\n133\ttargetRef selection, metadata verification on rollouts, degraded conditions on\n134\tunreachable A2A endpoints, sandbox auto-registration) are delivered by the\n135\tupstream operator's runtime behavior and are explicitly out of scope for this\n136\tstrategy (tracked by RHAIRFE-7587/7588/7589) — see Health Warnings.\n137\t\n138\t## Health Warnings\n139\t\n140\t- **Pending human reviews gate the whole strategy**: Architecture Review, Build\n141\t  Onboarding, License Validation, Documentation Support, and UXD Support are all\n142\t  \"Pending human review\" in the strategy's prerequisites table, and the Jira\n143\t  labels include `ac-review-pending` and `confidence-yellow`. Nothing in this\n144\t  DAG can substitute for those sign-offs.\n145\t- **Konflux submission lead time is a schedule risk, not an AC**: the risk table\n146\t  flags onboarding lead time against the code-complete deadline (submit\n147\t  immediately, escalate if delayed past 2 weeks before deadline). Captured as a\n148\t  risk note on the konflux-onboarding epics, not as an acceptance criterion.\n149\t- **Runtime acceptance criteria live outside this strategy**: the RFE-level\n150\t  MUSTs for discovery, metadata sync, and degraded conditions, and the COULD for\n151\t  sandbox auto-registration, are runtime operator behavior covered by\n152\t  RHAIRFE-7587/7588. No epic in this decomposition implements them; reviewers\n153\t  should not expect them here.\n154\t- **Top-level open questions treated as resolved or out of scope**: the\n155\t  pre-strategy \"Open Questions\" section asks about the minimal image contract\n156\t  format (A2A vs simpler) and the OpenShell Sandbox CR interaction. The refined\n157\t  technical approach pins the contract (capability description at\n158\t  `/.well-known/agent-card.json`, fetched by AgentRuntimeReconciler over mTLS,\n159\t  stored in AgentRuntime.Status.Card), and the Sandbox CR interaction is runtime\n160\t  behavior outside this strategy's productization scope. Neither changes the\n161\t  epic set; both are noted for the review record.\n162\t- **Priority observation**: the AuthBridge image HLR is P1 even though sidecar\n163\t  injection is part of the operator's TP function; this follows the strategy's\n164\t  own labels and is not an inversion introduced by decomposition.\n165\t- **Multiple gates on the DSC integration epic**: E011 is gated by three\n166\t  investigations (upstream validation, cleanup semantics, OTEL scope). The\n167\t  frontmatter `gated_by` field is single-valued by schema and holds only the\n168\t  primary gate (the upstream validation); the other two gates are recorded as\n169\t  dependencies and here. E011's `gate_failure_impact.fallback_approach`\n170\t  enumerates the outcome of all three gates so frontmatter consumers see the\n171\t  full rewrite surface, not just the primary one. The complete gate register\n172\t  (all Investigation → Implementation gates, primary and secondary):\n173\t\n174\t  | Gate | Gated epic | Recorded in `gated_by` | Action | Fallback summary |\n175\t  | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n176\t  | E001 (upstream validation / Keycloak) | E011 | yes (primary) | rewrite | Defer or remediate upstream controllers; deployment prerequisites change if Keycloak is required. |\n177\t  | E004 (AgentRuntime cleanup semantics) | E011 | no — schema holds one gate; edge + `fallback_approach` carry it | rewrite | Removed-state garbage-collection scope matches the decided boundary of operator-managed resources. |\n178\t  | E005 (OTEL trace sink scope) | E011 | no — schema holds one gate; edge + `fallback_approach` carry it | add_remediation | OTEL sink deployment configuration added if it enters TP scope. |\n179\t  | E002 (AuthBridge TP variant set) | E010 | yes | rewrite | One Konflux component per variant in the decided set. |\n180\t  | E002 (AuthBridge TP variant set) | E012 | yes | rewrite | One SHA256-pinned `RELATED_IMAGE_*` CSV entry per variant in the decided set. |\n181\t  | E003 (dashboard TP depth) | E013 | yes | rewrite | Agent-list tab vs standalone section changes the UI surface. |\n182\t\n183\t## Tiered Delivery\n184\t\n185\tNot applicable. The external dependencies (upstream kagenti-operator and\n186\tkagenti-extensions in the kagenti GitHub org, and the opendatahub-io midstream\n187\tforks) already exist per the strategy's dependency table — there is no\n188\tuncertain-timing external dependency requiring a Tier 1 / Tier 2 split. The\n189\tKonflux pipeline capacity concern is internal lead time (schedule risk), not an\n190\texternal dependency with uncertain acceptance timing.\n191\t\n192\t## Component Mappings (non-obvious)\n193\t\n194\tCanonical component names are taken verbatim from `.context/rhai-components.txt`:\n195\t\n196\t| Strategy component | Canonical Jira component | Note |\n197\t| --- | --- | --- |\n198\t| kagenti-operator | Agentic | No canonical component named for the kagenti project; `Agentic` is the closest match. Both kagenti repos map to it. |\n199\t| kagenti-extensions (AuthBridge) | Agentic | Same mapping; the two repos' epics are distinguished by team-identical but logically separate work (different repos). |\n200\t| rhods-operator | AI Core Platform | The platform's core operator managing DSC components. |\n201\t| odh-dashboard | AI Core Dashboard | The RHOAI web console. |\n202\t| QE (team, no component) | QE | Direct match. |\n203\t| Docs (team, no component) | Documentation | Direct match. |\n204\t\n205\t## Investigation Notes\n206\t\n207\t- Staff Engineer Input section is empty (template placeholder only) — no\n208\t  overrides to log.\n209\t- Five genuine unknowns were identified from the strategy's open-questions\n210\t  table, assumptions, and the \"Open\" acceptance-criteria note. The two\n211\t  open-questions-table items resolved by the same upstream validation experiment\n212\t  (controller functionality and the Keycloak runtime dependency / controller\n213\t  disablement) were combined into a single Investigation (E001) per the\n214\t  don't-split rule.\n215\t- No conditional branch files were created. The bounded-outcome investigations\n216\t  (AuthBridge variant set, OTEL scope, dashboard depth) all change the *scope*\n217\t  of an epic that exists in every outcome rather than selecting between\n218\t  different epic sets, so they are modeled as rewrite/add_remediation gates on\n219\t  the affected epics rather than branch epics.\n220\t- The sandbox auto-registration question and minimal image contract question\n221\t  (pre-strategy Open Questions) do not change which epics exist or what they do\n222\t  within this strategy's productization scope, so they are handled as noted in\n223\t  Health Warnings rather than as Investigations.\n224\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b1933c3e4a75d57c","agent_id":"a39dea4f4915a7ea0","session_id":"5aaaeded-1f18-481f-917f-f792958e6a2c","uuid":"5c928aa9-5869-49ec-b3cd-1deb91694b9c","timestamp":"2026-10-22T08:11:29.866Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-973951d2e757cc6a","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review revised decomposition"}
