t: the capability description endpoint format (`/.well-known/agent-card.json`), health check, and card structure (name, skills, protocols)\n51\t- Runtime prerequisites identified by the upstream validation (e.g., Keycloak, if required) and any OTEL trace sink integration in scope\n52\t- Disconnected/air-gapped installation notes for the kagenti-operator and AuthBridge images (mirroring via `RELATED_IMAGE_*`)\n53\t\n54\tWork scope:\n55\t\n56\t- Installation and upgrade documentation for enabling kagenti-operator via the DSC component\n57\t- The minimal image contract documentation (endpoint format, health check, card structure)\n58\t- Documentation of decided cleanup semantics on disable and of any runtime prerequisites and OTEL integration in Tech Preview scope\n59\t- All topics authored in the Red Hat docs content process\n60\t\n61\t## Acceptance Criteria\n62\t\n63\t- Documentation covers the minimal image contract for creating a discoverable agent (endpoint format, health check, card structure)\n64\t- Documentation covers enabling and disabling the kagenti-operator via the DSC, including the default-disabled Tech Preview posture\n65\t- Documentation is technically reviewed against the implemented behavior (component lifecycle, cleanup, prerequisites, and any OTEL integration) and reviewed for accuracy against the architecture context\n66\t- Documentation is published through the standard docs process\n67\t\n68\t## HLR Traceability\n69\t\n70\t- Strategy acceptance criterion (MUST): Documentation covers the minimal image contract for creating a discoverable agent (endpoint format, health check, card structure)\n71\t- Supports the P0 HLRs for DSC enablement/disable and TP opt-in (documents the user-facing procedure)\n72\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b1933c3e4a75d57c","agent_id":"a39dea4f4915a7ea0","session_id":"5aaaeded-1f18-481f-917f-f792958e6a2c","uuid":"8620478b-109a-4648-a9c3-d21a9de3eeb5","timestamp":"2026-10-22T08:11:58.918Z","tool_result_meta":[{"i