scheduling dependencies.\n\nMinor: E011 is gated by three Investigations (E001, E004, E005), but the\nfrontmatter `gated_by` field is single-valued by schema and holds only the\nprimary gate (E001). The secondary gates are carried by the dependency edges,\nthe summary's explicit gate register, and E011's `fallback_approach` (which\nenumerates all three outcomes), which is the best representation the schema\npermits — but a consumer reading only `gated_by` will under-detect gates on\nE011. Noted for the record; no metadata contract is violated.\n\n### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (2/2)\n\nType-appropriate signal fields are used throughout: E001-E005 (Investigation)\ncarry `investigation_signals` with `ai_signals: null`; E006-E015\n(Implementation) carry `ai_signals` with `investigation_signals: null`. All 15\n`-ai-signals.md` rationale files exist, and every rationale table matches the\nfrontmatter values (verified signal-by-signal for all 15 epics).\n\nRubric consistency spot-checks pass: the human-decision investigations\n(E002, E003, E005) correctly score `source_accessibility: 0` with\n`human_judgment_required: -2` (the answer is a pending PM/UX/team decision,\nnot a readable artifact); E001 and E004 correctly score `source_accessibility:\n1` (answers determined by public repos and documented platform patterns).\nImplementation signals track the strategy faithfully: `human_process_gates: -1`\non E008/E009/E010/E011/E013/E015 maps to the strategy's pending human reviews\n(license, Konflux submission, architecture review, UXD, docs review);\n`open_questions: -1` on E010/E011/E012/E013 maps to the gating investigations;\nE013's `change_specificity: 0` correctly reflects the unfixed TP UI surface.\nPer instructions, computed `ai_implementability`/`ai_implementability_score`\nvalues were not re-derived.\n\n### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\n\nEvery epic has testable ACs drawn from the strategy (kubectl-measurable\nlifecycle checks on E011, check-payload pass on E009/E010, mirror-registry\nresolution on E012/E014, rendered-list behavior on E013). Rule-mandated ACs\nare present wherever applicable: E015 (docs-authoring) has the technical\nreview AC; E009 and E010 (konflux chain) each have the build-pipeline-green\nAC; E013 has the feature-flag AC (UI hidden when component Removed). The\ncanonical soft-AC trap is avoided: the Konflux submission lead time is\nrecorded as a risk note (Health Warnings + E009 description), not as an AC.\nNo AC states an external schedule constraint as a success condition. No epic\nbody references sibling epics by draft ID (grep-verified; E-number references\nappear only in the summary, where they are the defined notation).\n\n### 7. Completeness (2/2)\n\nAll strategy scope is accounted for: Konflux onboarding of both image families\n(E009/E010), midstream forks (E006/E007), license validation (E008), DSC\ncomponent controller (E011), CSV packaging (E012), dashboard BFF + feature\nflag (E013), QE test plan + E2E incl. webhook ordering and disconnected\ninstall (E014), documentation incl. the minimal image contract (E015). All\nseven proposed strategy acceptance criteria map to epic ACs (AC1/AC3 → E011,\nAC2 → E014, AC4 → E009, AC5 → E010, AC6 → E013, AC7 → E012/E014). All five\nopen-questions-table items and the \"Open\" OTEL note became Investigations\n(E001-E005); the pre-strategy open questions are dispositioned in Health\nWarnings rather than silently dropped. Risks are carried forward (lead time,\nupstream gaps, webhook ordering, orphaned CRs, port collision). The\ndocs-authoring requirement (Documentation Support: Yes) is satisfied by E015.\nThe excluded runtime MUSTs are the strategy's own out-of-scope items\n(RHAIRFE-7587/7588/7589) and are explicitly flagged, not silently dropped.\n\nMinor: the container-security NFR (non-root USER 65532, capabilities.drop\nALL, seccompProfile RuntimeDefault) is explicitly scoped only in E009; E010\nand E013 (which also builds a container) rely implici